# width: 120
# height: 40
# `Ctrl+Q` on a CLEAN workspace stops to ask too — the fat-finger guard.
# The box is the quit's own, with [Q]uit / [C]ancel instead of the three
# buttons unsaved work gets, and Cancel holds the focus so Enter on a box
# nobody meant to raise is safe. Esc, Enter, `c` and a click on Cancel all
# leave the session exactly where it was.

write one.txt "one\n"
open one.txt
expect dirty false

key ctrl+q
expect screen contains "Quit mnml?"
expect screen contains "Nothing is unsaved. This closes mnml."
expect screen contains "[Q]uit"
expect screen contains "[C]ancel"
# // changed (one-confirm): one button row for every confirm — bracketed
# keys from the box's left edge, two cells apart.
expect screen contains "│   [Q]uit      [C]ancel                │"
# Nothing unsaved means nothing to save: the dirty box's buttons are not here.
expect screen lacks "[S]ave all"
expect screen lacks "[Q]uit anyway"

# Esc cancels; the workspace is still open.
key esc
expect screen lacks "Quit mnml?"
expect pane "one.txt"
expect screen contains "one"

# Enter lands on Cancel, because Cancel has the focus.
key ctrl+q
expect screen contains "Quit mnml?"
key enter
expect screen lacks "Quit mnml?"
expect pane "one.txt"

# `c` is Cancel's own letter.
key ctrl+q
expect screen contains "Quit mnml?"
key c
expect screen lacks "Quit mnml?"
expect pane "one.txt"

# The session is still usable after all that: the buffer still takes
# text, and Ctrl+Z puts it back so the workspace is clean again — the
# box below has to be the CLEAN one, not the unsaved-work box.
type " still here"
expect dirty true
expect screen contains " still hereone"
key ctrl+z
expect dirty false
expect screen lacks " still hereone"

# And the Quit button really is a quit. A click anywhere dismisses the
# box, so only this — the button's own row, and the app gone after it —
# tells a hit on `Quit` apart from a click that missed. x 45 is inside
# `  [Q]uit  `, which spans 41..50; the clean box's other button,
# `  [C]ancel  `, sits at 53..64. Row 15 is the button row (row 14 until
# the box became the one six-row shape).
# `expect quit` reads the App's own flag (the one the host stops on),
# rather than a spelling inside status.json's text. Nothing follows it:
# the runner stops stepping an App that has quit.
key ctrl+q
expect screen contains "Quit mnml?"
expect screen contains "Nothing is unsaved."
expect quit false
click 45 15
expect quit true
